From b10dd81a9dd574f3ac9305e067baa9fcce0b3714 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Broyojo <dha@xoba.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:30:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] FEXCore: Stop tracking a lookup cache's range before freeing
 it

A thread's lookup cache only reserves the memory for its L1 and L2
caches, and the frontend commits it page by page on access violations,
through the overcommit range the cache marks. The destructor freed the
reservation and then unmarked the range. A thread created in between
can be given the same addresses for its own lookup cache and mark them,
and the unmark then removes that thread's range: its next access to an
uncommitted page of its cache is no longer handled.

On Windows that access comes from FindBlock, inside CompileBlock, with
the code invalidation lock held. The frontend passes the fault on and
the process ends, or, when a memory notification holds
ThreadCreationMutex while it waits for the invalidation lock, the fault
handler waits for ThreadCreationMutex and both threads hang.

Unmark the range before freeing it.
---
 FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/LookupCache.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/LookupCache.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/LookupCache.cpp
index 0b230306f0..f030a42bc1 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/LookupCache.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/LookupCache.cpp
@@ -71,8 +71,9 @@ LookupCache::LookupCache(FEXCore::Context::ContextImpl* CTX)
 }
 
 LookupCache::~LookupCache() {
-  FEXCore::Allocator::VirtualFree(reinterpret_cast<void*>(PagePointer), TotalCacheSize);
+  // Stop tracking the range before freeing it: once it is free, another thread's lookup cache can be allocated there and mark it.
   ctx->SyscallHandler->UnmarkOvercommitRange(PagePointer, TotalCacheSize);
+  FEXCore::Allocator::VirtualFree(reinterpret_cast<void*>(PagePointer), TotalCacheSize);
 
   // No need to free BlockLinks map.
   // These will get freed when their memory allocators are deallocated.
